        "text_wUBUUw": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Tape can be made from a variety of materials, each of which has properties that make it suitable for different purposes. <a href=\"/collections/5-masking-paper-temporary-marking-labels\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Masking, Paper & Temporary Marking - LABELS\"><em>Paper tape</em>, often called<em> masking tape</em></a>, is a broad category of <a href=\"/collections/vinyl-aisle-floor-marking-adhesive-tape\" title=\"VINYL AISLE & FLOOR MARKING ADHESIVE TAPE\">adhesive tape</a> that can feature a variety of different types of paper, including, for example:</p><ul><li>Flatback paper</li><li>Crepe paper</li><li>Tissue paper</li><li>Fish paper</li><li>Kraft paper</li><li>Clay-coat paper</li></ul><p>These paper-backed tapes can be used in a <a href=\"/blogs/news/why-use-paper-tapes\" title=\"Why Use Paper Tapes?\">variety of applications</a>, from color-coding to splicing, mounting, and packaging. They come in all colors and can be designed to offer varying degrees of holding power, removability, and temperature-resistance.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base"
          }
        },
